# MediHuman Agent Rules

## Fast path
- Read `README.md` architecture section and `git status` before editing.
- Reproduce reported bug first; identify smallest responsible module.
- Make narrow patches. Preserve unrelated working-tree changes.
- Run `npm test`, relevant `node --check` commands, and `git diff --check`.
- Never claim browser, camera, Docker, or deployment checks unless actually run.

## Architecture boundaries
- `src/app.js`: composition entrypoint only.
- `src/client/state.js`: state shape and local storage (`medihuman.local-workspace.v3`).
- `src/client/views.js`: pure HTML rendering; no DOM writes or side effects.
- `src/client/controller.js`: events, API calls, camera/OCR, persistence orchestration.
- `src/client/ui.js`: escaping, buttons, notices, SVG primitives.
- `src/backend/api.js`: HTTP composition and route order only.
- `src/backend/routes/`: endpoint behavior by feature.
- `src/backend/auth.js`, `http.js`, `validation.js`, `records.js`: focused shared concerns.
- `styles.css`: stable entrypoint; keep `styles/*.css` import order: tokens → base → typography → layout → components → views → roles → utilities → responsive.

## Compatibility contracts
- Preserve `data-action`, `data-form`, DOM IDs, API paths/status/payloads, CSRF cookies, and role gates.
- Preserve local storage keys and v1→v2 backend migration behavior.
- New client modules must be added to `service-worker.js` shell cache.
- New CSS files must be copied by `Dockerfile` and served by the static server.

## Safety
- Never commit credentials, tokens, `.data/`, logs, or private patient data.
- Keep medication logic cautious and non-diagnostic.
- Doctors see records only after patient approval.
- Add tests for changed boundaries; prefer pure tests over dependencies.

## Git
- Use conventional commits: `fix:`, `feat:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`.
- Stage only intended files. Inspect status, diff, and recent log before commit.
- Push only when requested or when established task workflow requires it.
